The main claim that  $P$  is sent to  $X$ , the foot from  $D$  to  $EF$  under inversion about the incircle. To see this, note that  $(ABC)$  gets sent to the nine point circle of  $(ABC)$ , and  $(AEF)$  gets sent to  $EF$ , so their intersections post inversion are  $A'$  and  $X$ , where  $A'$  is the midpoint of  $EF$ . We see that  $A'$  is the image of  $A$ , so  $X$  must be the image of  $P$ .

Under inversion, the problem then reduces to showing that  $(DIX)$ ,  $(EIY)$ ,  $(FIZ)$  are coaxial, where  $XYZ$  is the orthic triangle of  $DEF$ . This is true because the orthocenter of  $DEF$  is clearly a point with equal power with respect to all  $3$ , and so is  $I$ , so they have a radical axis, as desired.

