\]

Starting with  $\Delta ACD$ , let  $|AC|=x$  such that by the Law of Cosines: $|AD|^2=|CD|^2+|AC|^2-2|CD||AC|\cos(30^{\circ} \Rightarrow 36=x^2+9-3\sqrt{3}x \Rightarrow x = \frac{3\sqrt{3} \pm 3\sqrt{15}}{2} \Rightarrow x = (3\sqrt{3})\phi$ ;

where  $\phi = $  the Golden Ratio.  Next, an application of the Law of Cosines to  $\Delta ABC$  yields: $|AB|^2= |BC|^2+|AC|^2-2|BC||AC|\cos(30^{\circ}) \Rightarrow |AB|^2 = 6^2+[(3\sqrt{3})\phi]^2-2(6)[(3\sqrt{3})\phi](\sqrt{3}/2) = 36+27\phi^{2}-54\phi$ .

Finally, another application of the Law of Cosines to  $\Delta ABD$  solves for  $\angle{ABD}=\theta$ : $\theta = \arccos\left(\frac{|AB|^2+|BD|^2-|AD|^2}{2|AB||BD|}\right) = \arccos\left[\frac{(36+27\phi^{2}-54\phi)+9-36}{2(\sqrt{36+27\phi^{2}-54\phi})(3)}\right] = \textcolor{red}{107^{\circ}}$ .

