Note that  $\triangle AGD$  and  $\triangle CFE$  are 30-60-90 triangles. Therefore,  $AD = CE = \sqrt{3}*1 = \sqrt{3}$ . Denote the midpoint of  $\overline{FG}$  as  $M$ , and the midpoint of  $\overline{DE}$  as  $N$ . Also, note that  $GM = FM = 1$ , so  $DN = EN = 1$ . So the side length is  $1+1+\sqrt{3}+\sqrt{3}=2+2\sqrt{3}$ . (I believe that ryanbear calculated the side length correctly, but probably forgot to calculate the area after this.)Finally, substituting this into the area for a equilateral triangle from the side length formula, we get that the area is  $\boxed{6+4\sqrt{3}}$ .</details>

